{
  "_comment": "Canonical mesh/device wire samples for Bridge Protocol v1: registration bodies, device/location shapes, the full device_command surface with canonical params, and command-result shapes. `nodeDesktopCapabilities` are node commands only some platforms implement (today: `computer` on macOS), advertised on top of `nodeCapabilities` where available. Asserted by all three implementations — the daemon validates registrations/locations through its real normalizers (protocol-conformance.test.ts), talon-node executes the `run: true` commands through its real dispatch and asserts capability parity (protocol_conformance_test.go), and the companion asserts capability parity and runs the DeviceExec subset (protocol_conformance_test.dart). `{{TMP}}` in params is replaced by each executor test with a sandbox directory it seeds from `sandboxFiles`. `dataKeys` lists result-data keys BOTH device implementations must produce for that command — the daemon's tools read these names. `transfer: true` marks the streamed transfer commands: each suite serves `transferBody` for the push token and accepts the pull upload on a fake /devices/file, then checks the `sha256` both ways (the push param is the body's digest; the device reports the digest of what it moved).",
